Three tests fail, for two different reasons.

- **Two expectations were my mistake.** A terminal event goes to `onDone`, not `onState`, so `states` correctly stops at `lastSeq` 2. I'll assert on `done[0].lastSeq` in those tests.
- **One is a real bug.** After a gap, the gap flag stays set. A second gap on the new stream returns the same state object, so `receive` returns early and never reconnects. Duplicates on the new stream would also be misread as gaps. The fix is to check `next.gap` before the identity check, and clear the flag when reopening.[INFO] [KRS] <-- GenerateAssistantResponseCommand done totalEvents=458

